  "body": "First production-readiness upgrade after released v0.28.0.\n\nScope is deliberately limited to the first roadmap step: **coverage/gaps**.\n\nAdds:\n- automatic `coverage_report.json/md` and `gaps.json/md` on ordinary scans;\n- explicit `scan-body coverage-gaps DB --out-dir DIR` regeneration command;\n- exact coverage-state rollups across canonical files/nodes/edges/findings/semantic graph/completeness;\n- surface and effect closure summaries;\n- unresolved acquisition/parser/node/edge/finding/completeness/surface/effect gap records with canonical IDs and evidence IDs;\n- no scalar confidence score;\n- no priority/ranking;\n- no evidence promotion or canonical writes;\n- deterministic/read-only invariants and reconciliation tests.\n\nv0.28 remains untouched and sealed. v0.29 intentionally has no package manifest yet.\n\nNext roadmap stages (uncertainty challenger, triage ranking, layered provenance, parity scenarios, broader calibration, reconstruction/runtime/hardening) are explicitly out of scope for this PR.",
